1 PSL
    The PSL is a 32-bit integer value stored in the processor.  The SHOW PSL
    command can be used to display the PSL as an integer, and also as the
    individual fields of the PSL.  These fields are:

    C       carry bit
    V       overflow bit
    Z       zero value
    N       negative value
    T       trace pending
    IV      integer overflow
    FU      floating point underflow
    DV      divide-by-zero
    IPL     current interrupt priority level
    MOD     current mode (user, kernel, supervisor, executive)
